WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.492
On this slide, we are focusing on preview a conversion error.

00:00:03.492 --> 00:00:08.152
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.152 --> 00:00:14.042
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.042 --> 00:00:18.777
A conversion error tells us the input does not satisfy our assumption.

00:00:18.777 --> 00:00:25.187
Real analytical workflows validate messy input instead of silently pretending it is correct.

00:00:25.187 --> 00:00:28.372
Connect the concept to a small analytics task.

00:00:28.372 --> 00:00:33.447
Imagine the value came from a sales file, survey, or operational system.

00:00:33.447 --> 00:00:38.462
Ask whether Python is interpreting it correctly and whether another person could understand the calculation

00:00:38.462 --> 00:00:40.877
from the names and output.
